# Kart driver enlarged relative to the kart ? 2026-11-12

KRS01?KRS03 address the owner's clarification that the driver looks small relative to the kart in a race. The camera and kart scale remain unchanged. The native helmet grows 20% in each dimension; the upper torso becomes taller and up to 18% broader at the shoulders. Sleeves gain volume and are refitted from the wider, higher shoulders toward the existing elbows. Distal forearm axes and glove grips remain fitted. The seated crown rises 106.3 mm in model space; this is not a 20% scale applied to the entire driver.

Matched native comparisons: [before close-up](evidence/kart-driver-race-scale-2026-11-12/before-body.png), [larger driver](evidence/kart-driver-race-scale-2026-11-12/after-body.png), [before overhead](evidence/kart-driver-race-scale-2026-11-12/before-overhead.png), [larger overhead](evidence/kart-driver-race-scale-2026-11-12/after-overhead.png). Actual race, one frozen scene: [original driver](evidence/kart-driver-race-scale-2026-11-12/app-gl-repeat/race-before-size.png), [enlarged driver](evidence/kart-driver-race-scale-2026-11-12/app-gl-repeat/race.png). Both race images use identical camera, kart transform, scene and HUD.

The actual Compatibility race measures the helmet from approximately **6.521 ? 6.163 pixels to 7.826 ? 7.395 pixels** at 1280 ? 720. Both dimensions increase 20%, giving about 44% more projected helmet area. This is measured geometry projection, not a visibility/pixel-segmentation score. The race camera extent stays 30.434782; the car node scale stays (0.88, 0.88, 0.88) and the driver node scale stays (1, 1, 1). The enlargement is baked into anatomy and appears consistently in the Garage and race, rather than being a race-only transform.

The driver remains **12,480 triangles / six material roles / six steering poses**, with moving cloth/gloves and four separate static helmet surfaces. The raw glove vertex/attribute/index/morph packets are exact. Cloth topology, colours and UVs remain exact. All 1,102 tested lower-body and supported-back vertices remain at their fitted positions. The hips, knees, boot soles, hand targets and wheel/pedal locations stay fixed. The continuous shoulders, straight limb shafts and compact elbows remain; the wrist axes are preserved.

The independent anatomy regression passes **41/0** and rejects the original small-driver control **41/3**. It measures saved native bounds and unchanged-camera projection, checks protected vertices and raw glove packets, equal pose topology, culling bounds, finite normals and straight arm shafts. Actual cockpit/backrest checks pass **286/0**, pedal/pan/grip contact **27/0**, moving hood/side-pod clearance **270/0**, and the relocated fuel assembly's all-pose/obstacle matrix **790/0**.

